{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem (operator-directed, live repro 2026-08-14)\nClosing deadbeat-warlike-ostrich (8d74, budget recalibration) failed with \"insufficient-evidence: the bounded evidence search was exhausted before evidence was found — this is search exhaustion, not refutation; nothing was positively refuted\", and the remedy text asks the OPERATOR to post evidence comments and re-run. Operator ruling: search exhaustion is a problem the gate should automatically resolve, not one that should require operator attestation or manual retry.\n\n## Why auto-resolution is already cheap\nThe machinery landed today (Gerrit 1796): per-criterion PASS verdicts are banked within a run and persisted to the cross-run cache keyed by (criterion-hash, ref-scoped file_impact blob fingerprint). A second verification pass seeds all prior PASSes (\"already credited — do not re-verify\") and spends its ENTIRE budget on the insufficient criteria only. The close simply does not invoke that second pass itself — it fails and prints instructions.\n\n## Fix\nIn the completion close gate: when a verification verdict FAILS with one or more insufficient-evidence criteria AND zero refuted criteria, automatically resume — re-run verification (cache seeds the credited PASSes; budget re-derives over the REMAINING criteria via verify_step_floor) up to a bounded resumption count (config key, default 2 resumptions). Surface to the operator only when (a) a criterion is positively REFUTED, or (b) a criterion remains insufficient after the final resumption — and only then print the evidence-comment remedy. Emit one stderr progress line per resumption (\"resuming verification: N criteria remain, M credited\"). Operation-linked and in-process — no CI/scheduler dependency (project.portability).\n\n## Search-frontier handoff (operator-directed)\nEach resumption receives a deterministic digest of the prior pass's search frontier, extracted from the runner's tool-call transcript for the still-insufficient criteria:\n- NEGATIVE frontier: paths read / searches run that yielded no evidence — injected as ADVISORY steering (\"already searched, nothing found there; prioritize unsearched locations; revisit only with a specific new reason\"), never a hard exclusion (a hard exclusion would turn a soft miss into a permanent blind spot).\n- POSITIVE frontier: where evidence for the CREDITED criteria was found — sibling ACs cluster (module + its tests), so this steers the retry to the productive neighborhood first.\nNegative knowledge is valid only within the close (same pinned ref across resumptions); it is NOT persisted to the cross-run cache.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Resumption only on exhaustion-without-refutation; a refuted criterion fails fast (no retry laundering).\n- Each resumption is budget-bounded by the existing floor/clamp arithmetic; the resumption COUNT is the new bound. No unbounded loops: worst case = (1 + max_resumptions) verifier invocations per close.\n- Cache/bank staleness rules unchanged (blob-fingerprint + ref binding decide reuse; this feature adds no new reuse path).\n- not_a_bug/disposition/forced closes unaffected.\n\n## Relation to the north star\nInterim symptom relief consistent with viral-peppy-lowchen (evidence-prepacked single-pass verifier): prepacking removes the SEARCH from the verifier so exhaustion stops occurring; this ticket makes the gate self-healing until that lands, and its resumption loop remains useful as the dumb backstop afterward.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A close whose first verification ends with insufficient-evidence-only unmet criteria (no refutations) automatically re-verifies, seeding cached PASSes, without operator action (integration test with a stubbed runner scripted to exhaust on pass 1 and pass on pass 2).\n- [ ] A refuted criterion fails the close immediately with no resumption (test).\n- [ ] Resumption count bounded by a config key (default 2); exceeding it surfaces the current remedy text (test).\n- [ ] Resumption prompt carries the frontier digest: negative frontier advisory-phrased, positive frontier present when any criterion was credited; extraction is deterministic from the transcript (unit test on the extractor + prompt-block test).\n- [ ] Progress lines on stderr name remaining vs credited counts per resumption (test).\n- [ ] `make lint`/`make typecheck` clean.\n- [ ] Lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786760029952919001,"uuid":"d3d79649-676a-46e8-bd63-54dd1dc7ec4c"}